WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.387
This is the wrap-up for Module 6.

00:00:02.387 --> 00:00:05.632
The main theme of this module is organization.

00:00:05.632 --> 00:00:13.537
As analytics programs become larger, code organization becomes just as important as individual lines of

00:00:13.537 --> 00:00:19.472
syntax. Modules allow us to import reusable tools so we do not rewrite common code.

00:00:19.472 --> 00:00:23.797
Packages group related modules when a project grows larger.

00:00:23.797 --> 00:00:28.087
Classes allow us to store related data and behavior together.

00:00:28.087 --> 00:00:32.857
We also learned that objects are individual examples created from a class,

00:00:32.857 --> 00:00:36.222
and methods are functions that belong to a class.

00:00:36.222 --> 00:00:40.297
A key practical skill is knowing when to use each tool.

00:00:40.297 --> 00:00:43.082
Use functions for reusable tasks.

00:00:43.082 --> 00:00:45.817
Use dictionaries for related values.

00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:49.382
Use classes when data and actions belong together.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:55.067
Use modules and packages to organize reusable code across files and folders.

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.577
For practice, try creating a StudentScore class.

00:00:56.577 --> 00:01:01.072
It could store a student's name and a list of scores.

00:01:01.072 --> 00:01:06.392
Then it could include a method that returns the average score.

00:01:06.392 --> 00:01:11.062
After that, create two student objects and print their averages.

00:01:11.062 --> 00:01:14.322
The main skill is not memorizing syntax.

00:01:14.322 --> 00:01:19.252
The main skill is learning how to keep code organized as an analytics project grows.
